## 🔑 Key Design Decisions

**Why no shuffle in train/test split?**
Financial time series has autocorrelation — shuffling leaks future information into training. We use strict temporal split + walk-forward CV.

**Why XGBoost over LSTM for daily data?**
With 2,500 training rows (10 years daily), gradient boosting on well-engineered features outperforms LSTM which needs 100k+ sequences to learn effectively.

**Why 0.1% transaction cost?**
NSE charges: 0.03% brokerage + 0.025% STT + 0.00325% exchange = ~0.058% one-way, ~0.116% round-trip. We use 0.1% as a conservative estimate.

**Sharpe interpretation:**
- < 0.5: Poor — don't deploy
- 0.5–1.0: Acceptable
- 1.0–2.0: Good — Buffett's lifetime Sharpe ≈ 0.76
- > 2.0: Excellent

